WEBVTT

00:56.257 --> 00:58.968
FILING FOR LOVE

01:04.640 --> 01:06.392
Is he still waiting
in the emergency room?

01:10.312 --> 01:12.565
No, there's no need.
I'll call you back.

01:12.940 --> 01:14.358
I'll just get off here.

01:14.984 --> 01:17.528
It's still pretty far from here.
Just past the intersection...

01:17.778 --> 01:19.196
In-a!

02:37.608 --> 02:39.485
Excuse me. Nurse?

02:39.568 --> 02:41.236
Doesn't he need surgery right away?

02:41.320 --> 02:42.655
Why is there a delay?

02:42.738 --> 02:44.531
Let me find out. Just a moment.

02:47.409 --> 02:49.161
Don't we have any available OR yet?

02:49.244 --> 02:51.830
They're full. The one that's left
is being prepped for a VIP.

02:51.914 --> 02:53.874
- Why?
- Then

02:54.166 --> 02:55.876
can't you organize
a transfer or a temporary OR?

02:56.460 --> 02:59.380
Do something!
You can't just leave him here!

03:01.215 --> 03:02.216
In-a.

03:03.801 --> 03:05.469
You can help, Jae-yeol, can't you?

03:05.552 --> 03:07.179
Call someone at Haemu Hospital.

03:07.262 --> 03:09.473
Please, I beg of you. Help him out.

03:14.728 --> 03:16.855
TIME IN SURGERY

03:16.939 --> 03:18.440
TIME IN SURGERY, ANESTHETIC DURATION
CURRENT TIME

03:32.246 --> 03:35.499
Out of all the trauma surgeons,
Dr. Yoon is the best.

03:35.582 --> 03:36.875
Don't you worry.

03:36.959 --> 03:38.627
I'll keep an eye on the patient, too.

03:39.336 --> 03:41.296
- Thank you, director.
- Bye, then.

03:49.179 --> 03:51.765
OPERATION ROOM

05:23.273 --> 05:25.609
Mr. Noh, are you awake?

05:25.692 --> 05:26.693
Mr. Noh.

05:54.596 --> 05:58.141
EPISODE 8:
DESIRE &amp; HOPE

05:58.225 --> 06:00.185
HAEMU GENERAL HOSPITAL

06:00.269 --> 06:01.645
I'm coming for you!

06:01.728 --> 06:03.564
- Stop!
- No!

06:05.774 --> 06:07.276
Catch me if you can!

06:08.777 --> 06:10.779
Do you think this is
some kids' playground?

06:11.196 --> 06:12.990
I'm a patient, okay?

06:13.657 --> 06:16.994
I need some peace and quiet to rest!

06:17.077 --> 06:19.913
Hey, we brought you
some expensive food, so eat it!

06:19.997 --> 06:22.374
No, thanks. I lost my appetite.
You can eat it all.

06:23.292 --> 06:25.669
You poor thing. You have no appetite?

06:26.336 --> 06:28.755
Tell me if there's anything you want.
I'll make it for you.

06:29.089 --> 06:30.465
By the way...

06:30.591 --> 06:32.426
I haven't seen that lady recently.

06:32.509 --> 06:34.344
The head of your department.

06:34.803 --> 06:35.804
You're right.

06:35.888 --> 06:38.640
When you were unconscious,
she came by all the time

06:38.724 --> 06:41.393
and wouldn't stop looking at you
with those forlorn eyes.

06:41.476 --> 06:43.228
I haven't seen her since you woke up.

06:44.187 --> 06:48.025
Do you think you'd feel better
if she were to visit?

06:48.442 --> 06:50.903
You woke up when she was with you.

06:50.986 --> 06:51.987
Hey.

06:52.362 --> 06:53.780
What's going on between you two?

06:54.323 --> 06:56.074
She didn't seem like just a coworker.

06:56.408 --> 06:57.701
There's more to it, isn't there?

06:59.077 --> 07:00.162
She's not just your boss.

07:00.245 --> 07:02.372
She's your sweet darling, isn't she?

07:04.833 --> 07:07.377
Will you stay out of my business?

07:08.503 --> 07:11.131
Is my little brother embarrassed?

07:11.214 --> 07:14.092
Oh, you cutie pie.

07:15.177 --> 07:16.553
What's wrong with you?

08:05.852 --> 08:07.062
That smells amazing.

08:18.782 --> 08:21.118
You treat me like
I'm your errand girl.

08:21.201 --> 08:23.245
Who craves a toasted sandwich
at the crack of dawn?

08:23.328 --> 08:24.997
It made you come to see me.

08:25.539 --> 08:27.124
I came by because I was afraid.

08:27.207 --> 08:29.376
Who sends over 20 texts
asking for a toasted sandwich?

08:29.459 --> 08:31.753
What were you so afraid of
when I was unconscious

08:31.837 --> 08:37.259
that made you look after me
around the clock for days?

08:39.594 --> 08:40.846
My sisters told me all about it.

08:41.888 --> 08:43.974
They said they were moved to tears.

08:47.352 --> 08:48.353
I was afraid.

08:51.481 --> 08:52.566
It was scary.

08:55.152 --> 08:56.361
And also...

08:57.237 --> 08:59.573
As your superior,
I should look out for you.

08:59.656 --> 09:00.949
I was just checking in

09:01.033 --> 09:02.200
to see if you were dead or alive.

09:14.671 --> 09:18.383
Sure, I bet you were just looking out
for an employee.

09:19.342 --> 09:21.053
But since you're looking out
for me anyway

09:22.262 --> 09:24.222
could you get me discharged
and take me home?

09:25.891 --> 09:27.893
- You're asking me to do that?
- Yes.

09:34.399 --> 09:37.152
Handle that box with care.

09:37.235 --> 09:38.945
There are quite a few breakables.

09:39.362 --> 09:42.199
Why is there so much luggage
when you were stuck in a ward?

09:42.866 --> 09:45.494
They deliver all sorts of things
to hospitals these days.

09:50.332 --> 09:52.167
What am I even doing here?

09:53.752 --> 09:56.379
Why should I get you discharged
and take you home, too?

09:56.755 --> 09:58.673
I still have stitches in my stomach

09:58.757 --> 10:01.259
and I have so much stuff
with no one else to help.

10:01.760 --> 10:04.262
Isn't this the least you can do
for your staff?

10:07.099 --> 10:08.225
Wait and see.

10:08.308 --> 10:09.684
As soon as those stitches come out

10:09.768 --> 10:13.146
I'll make you work extra hard
to make up for the time you wasted.

10:13.647 --> 10:14.689
Sure.

10:15.190 --> 10:16.733
That's the truth.

10:17.109 --> 10:19.694
That area is very undervalued.

10:20.112 --> 10:22.197
You think redevelopment is old news

10:22.280 --> 10:23.782
but land always retains its value.

10:24.199 --> 10:25.408
It does.

10:26.284 --> 10:28.662
Do something!
You can't just leave him here!

10:28.912 --> 10:31.289
Please, I beg of you. Help him out.

10:35.001 --> 10:36.211
Don't you agree, Jae-yeol?

10:38.255 --> 10:40.298
- I'm not sure.
- Goodness...

10:40.966 --> 10:43.593
He never gets the timing right.

10:43.885 --> 10:47.013
You seem to be against the idea
of turning that place upside-down.

10:47.848 --> 10:50.851
A lot of people would lose
their homes and livelihoods.

10:51.017 --> 10:52.352
They get compensated for that.

10:52.644 --> 10:54.062
We don't kick them out penniless.

10:54.563 --> 10:57.691
My brother is so softhearted.

10:58.275 --> 11:01.236
He could never turn a blind eye
to people in need since he was young.

11:01.319 --> 11:03.947
He always makes a sacrifice
or gives up what's his.

11:04.406 --> 11:06.867
The Jeons are known to be ruthless.
You know what my father's like.

11:06.950 --> 11:08.618
He's the most ruthless businessman
in the country.

11:11.454 --> 11:14.291
I just don't get
who Jae-yeol takes after.

11:14.374 --> 11:15.500
What I do know

11:15.959 --> 11:17.502
is that he's not like our father.

11:19.421 --> 11:20.881
He must be like his mom.

11:41.902 --> 11:43.862
Sorry. I apologize instead.

11:43.945 --> 11:45.238
He had too much to drink.

11:47.157 --> 11:49.451
I contacted the PR Team. Get his car.

11:49.534 --> 11:50.911
I'll bring the VP downstairs now.

12:04.466 --> 12:05.842
Hello, A-jeong.

12:06.593 --> 12:08.011
Why are you acting out of character?

12:10.222 --> 12:12.933
You can't lash out like this
when a board meeting's coming up.

12:14.851 --> 12:16.436
Will you let me off today?

12:25.570 --> 12:26.655
Joo In-a...

12:27.906 --> 12:30.283
What on earth is she to you?

12:33.119 --> 12:35.330
She's someone I would die with.

12:43.088 --> 12:45.924
How could you not keep an umbrella
in your car for emergencies?

12:47.175 --> 12:50.053
I should get one for you
for next time.

12:53.390 --> 12:55.976
If A-jeong's home,
why don't you ask her to bring one?

12:56.893 --> 12:58.520
Why should we bother her?

12:59.437 --> 13:01.648
It's a passing shower.
I'll wait until it stops raining.

13:07.112 --> 13:08.905
Why did you and A-jeong break up?

13:10.156 --> 13:11.574
I don't exactly know why.

13:11.658 --> 13:13.451
She ghosted me out of the blue.

13:14.035 --> 13:15.578
Didn't you ask her why?

13:15.662 --> 13:16.830
You must've seen her at work.

13:17.497 --> 13:18.540
I didn't ask.

13:19.874 --> 13:21.626
I assumed there was a reason
she didn't tell me.

13:26.881 --> 13:27.924
Why do you ask?

13:28.717 --> 13:31.886
Would you have asked
if you were in my place?

13:34.597 --> 13:35.765
If that had been me...

13:36.850 --> 13:38.351
If I were A-jeong

13:40.687 --> 13:42.147
I would have wanted you to ask.

13:45.734 --> 13:48.361
Oddly enough, I have a habit

13:48.653 --> 13:50.322
of hiding the truth
when it matters most.

13:51.781 --> 13:53.283
While on the inside

13:54.576 --> 13:56.578
I hope someone
would drag the truth out of me.

13:57.662 --> 13:59.831
I hope someone
wouldn't give up on me.

14:00.832 --> 14:03.043
I get selfish and contradictory.

14:06.671 --> 14:10.008
Wouldn't it be easier
just to be honest?

14:14.179 --> 14:15.347
Do you mean that?

14:15.889 --> 14:17.015
So what?

14:17.349 --> 14:19.934
- You want me to get married?
- Yes, I mean it.

14:20.143 --> 14:22.562
Should we elope or something?

14:23.021 --> 14:24.939
And get disowned and lose everything?

14:26.149 --> 14:28.735
- I don't want that kind of life.
- In-a.

14:28.818 --> 14:29.986
Either way

14:30.528 --> 14:32.864
I was never naive enough
to think what we had

14:33.907 --> 14:35.325
would last forever.

14:36.034 --> 14:38.703
You can get married freely.
There's no need to feel guilty.

14:39.204 --> 14:40.413
I really am

14:41.331 --> 14:42.540
okay with it.

14:49.881 --> 14:54.010
I think it's because
I don't know how to be happy.

14:58.807 --> 15:01.684
Just when I think I'm happy,
I feel uneasy and anxious.

15:02.268 --> 15:03.937
I ask myself,
"Do I even deserve this?"

15:05.271 --> 15:06.439
I get afraid.

15:06.815 --> 15:08.316
I hide and run away.

15:10.110 --> 15:11.986
I'm just more used to being unhappy.

15:19.494 --> 15:20.662
Close your eyes.

15:21.830 --> 15:23.206
- What for?
- Come on.

15:23.790 --> 15:26.418
I won't do anything weird.
Relax and close your eyes.

15:30.588 --> 15:31.589
Okay.

15:32.882 --> 15:34.175
What do you hear?

15:35.552 --> 15:37.011
I hear the rain. What else?

15:37.095 --> 15:40.181
Calm yourself and focus
on the sounds around you.

15:54.112 --> 15:56.990
The sound of raindrops
hitting the windows.

15:57.907 --> 15:58.992
And?

15:59.868 --> 16:00.994
"And"?

16:02.328 --> 16:04.330
- The car's engine.
- And?

16:08.001 --> 16:09.669
A passing motorcycle.

16:11.421 --> 16:12.464
What else?

16:17.510 --> 16:18.595
Kids laughing

16:19.554 --> 16:20.722
in the distance.

16:22.056 --> 16:23.099
And?

16:26.436 --> 16:27.729
The sound of your breath.

16:28.646 --> 16:29.689
And?

16:35.361 --> 16:36.571
My heartbeat.

16:42.452 --> 16:44.037
That's how you feel it.

16:47.081 --> 16:50.335
If you look within yourself
just hard enough

16:51.169 --> 16:52.629
with all your heart

16:55.006 --> 16:56.299
happiness is right there.

16:58.051 --> 16:59.594
It's always there

17:00.428 --> 17:01.638
so whenever you want to find it

17:04.098 --> 17:05.308
do what you did just now.

17:37.423 --> 17:38.967
Welcome back!

17:39.676 --> 17:41.511
- Glad you're okay.
- Thank you.

17:42.804 --> 17:44.639
You had a tough time, Mr. Noh.

17:45.056 --> 17:46.432
But you look

17:47.016 --> 17:48.393
even better than before.

17:48.476 --> 17:49.811
Did the hospital food
suit your taste?

17:50.645 --> 17:53.106
He looks better
because he was away from work.

17:53.189 --> 17:54.899
Don't be silly.

17:54.983 --> 17:57.402
Mr. Noh always looked good.

17:57.485 --> 18:00.029
The office is brighter
now that you're back.

18:00.113 --> 18:01.197
Welcome back.

18:01.489 --> 18:04.784
I missed you so very much, Mr. Noh.

18:05.410 --> 18:06.953
Don't go overboard.

18:07.537 --> 18:09.622
You don't have to worry
about Mr. Ahn.

18:09.706 --> 18:13.918
Legal is taking an aggressive stance.
He'll pay a hefty price.

18:14.002 --> 18:16.212
It looks like his family
cut ties with him, too.

18:16.296 --> 18:18.256
He brought it upon himself.
You did well, Mr. Noh.

18:18.840 --> 18:19.882
Thanks.

18:19.966 --> 18:21.968
Your teammates must love you.

18:22.051 --> 18:24.012
You didn't want to transfer
in the beginning, though.

18:24.429 --> 18:27.307
- You wanted to transfer.
- Yes, more than anything.

18:27.390 --> 18:29.017
Yes, that's true.

18:29.559 --> 18:31.060
Good morning, Ms. Joo.

18:32.228 --> 18:33.771
- Hello.
- Morning.

18:33.980 --> 18:35.398
You're back, Mr. Noh.

18:35.773 --> 18:37.442
Yes, I'm back, Ms. Joo.

18:37.525 --> 18:40.069
Ms. Joo.
Do you have special plans for later?

18:40.153 --> 18:42.655
You look nicer than usual.
I almost didn't recognize you.

18:46.743 --> 18:49.370
Are you saying I looked dowdy before?

18:49.871 --> 18:52.123
No, that's not what I meant.

18:52.206 --> 18:54.167
You must be in a good mood
for some reason.

18:54.250 --> 18:56.169
Could it be the return
of your favorite employee?

18:56.753 --> 18:58.963
- I don't expect a lavish welcome...
- Mr. Noh.

19:01.716 --> 19:05.053
You lost touch with how things are
while you were away.

19:09.682 --> 19:11.684
I should help you return to reality.

19:18.816 --> 19:21.736
I guess Ms. Joo still dislikes you.

19:22.487 --> 19:24.447
I think the stabbing
didn't really change anything.

19:28.701 --> 19:29.786
It's fine.

19:30.119 --> 19:31.412
This is nothing.

19:32.080 --> 19:33.873
I'm Noh Ki-jun,
the ace of the Audit Team.

19:35.249 --> 19:36.376
Thanks.

19:36.959 --> 19:38.503
Okay, let's do this.

20:03.778 --> 20:06.614
I finished all the tasks you gave me.

20:07.740 --> 20:09.117
AUDIT TEAM HEAD JOO IN-A

20:09.200 --> 20:10.368
OK

20:11.577 --> 20:13.121
"OK"?

20:17.583 --> 20:19.293
This is too much.

20:23.256 --> 20:25.883
This is too much.
My first day after a stabbing...

20:29.804 --> 20:31.556
You worked hard today.
I'll treat you to a meal.

20:32.390 --> 20:34.225
You will? When?

20:35.101 --> 20:41.899
AUDIT TEAM HEAD JOO IN-A

20:50.074 --> 20:52.368
Friday evening. Come to my place.

20:58.666 --> 20:59.834
What's the matter?

21:03.045 --> 21:05.089
- It's my back.
- Is your back sore?

21:28.196 --> 21:29.322
Mr. Noh.

21:29.989 --> 21:31.449
Hey, Doo-gi.

21:31.991 --> 21:34.452
I'm sorry I couldn't visit you
in the hospital.

21:35.620 --> 21:36.746
Don't be.

21:37.413 --> 21:40.208
I won't visit you in the hospital
if you ever get stabbed.

21:40.291 --> 21:41.375
We're even.

21:42.376 --> 21:43.586
Fine, whatever.

21:45.546 --> 21:49.050
Oh, right.
I have a work-related question.

21:49.133 --> 21:51.969
- Yes?
- You handled Haemu Pharmaceutical.

21:52.345 --> 21:53.429
Yes, I did.

21:53.513 --> 21:56.015
Were you working
on anything in particular?

21:56.724 --> 21:58.351
What are you talking about?

21:58.684 --> 22:01.145
I handed over all the files.
Didn't you check the cloud server?

22:01.479 --> 22:05.358
Yes, I did,
but I didn't find anything.

22:05.942 --> 22:07.777
- Was the folder empty?
- Yes.

22:10.822 --> 22:13.115
- I'll check and get back to you.
- Okay.

22:23.209 --> 22:25.920
It's an important audit
on one of our subsidiaries.

22:26.003 --> 22:27.129
Let me finish it.

22:27.213 --> 22:29.423
Put all the info on our cloud server.

22:29.507 --> 22:31.175
I'll take a look
and allocate someone else.

22:35.638 --> 22:38.599
NOH KI-JUN'S PROJECT TRANSFER

22:38.683 --> 22:41.143
NO FILES OR FOLDERS
NAMED NOH KI-JUN'S PROJECT TRANSFER

22:50.570 --> 22:52.029
Hey, Jae-hong. Are you busy?

22:53.072 --> 22:54.615
I need a favor.

22:55.032 --> 22:58.452
A folder I uploaded
to our cloud server vanished.

23:05.668 --> 23:07.086
RICE
20KG

23:07.837 --> 23:09.672
Yes, this is perfect.

23:20.808 --> 23:21.976
Can I help you?

23:22.476 --> 23:24.186
Oh, yes.

23:24.604 --> 23:27.857
What would you recommend
to give someone who is recovering?

23:27.940 --> 23:29.025
Korean beef is the best.

23:29.108 --> 23:30.484
What are you going to cook?

23:31.193 --> 23:34.196
What dish looks difficult
but easy to cook

23:34.280 --> 23:36.532
and looks complicated
but simple to prepare?

23:37.867 --> 23:40.077
Just give me everything here.

23:40.578 --> 23:42.747
- All of this?
- I need to practice.

23:43.080 --> 23:44.165
Okay.

23:54.175 --> 23:56.802
That folder was deleted
two days later.

23:57.303 --> 23:58.763
It was accessed from Joo In-a's desk.

24:14.654 --> 24:16.030
HAEMU PHARMACEUTICAL

24:20.076 --> 24:22.078
CONFIRMATION NEEDED,
HAEMU PHARMA BUSINESS REPORT

24:23.621 --> 24:24.956
BUSINESS REPORT

24:25.039 --> 24:26.499
HAEMU PHARMACEUTICAL INC.,
CEO JEON JAE-YEOL

24:31.504 --> 24:33.464
Put the garlic cloves sideways.

24:33.547 --> 24:35.383
This is whole fresh garlic.

24:35.675 --> 24:37.760
We'll cut them in half as well.

24:37.843 --> 24:40.429
It won't taste as good
if the slices are too thin.

24:40.513 --> 24:43.849
The more garlic
you use in this recipe

24:43.933 --> 24:47.103
the more flavor
and health benefits there are.

24:49.563 --> 24:50.564
Let's see...

24:57.530 --> 25:00.199
Put the pot on the cooker

25:00.282 --> 25:02.076
- and add two spoons of sesame oil.
- Add oil...

25:02.284 --> 25:05.955
- Wait. Sesame oil.
- One spoonful of garlic.

25:06.497 --> 25:08.499
Sesame oil. I don't have any oil.

25:09.333 --> 25:11.085
CANOLA OIL, GROUND GARLIC,
PERILLA SEED OIL, SESAME OIL

25:16.298 --> 25:17.425
All right.

26:05.264 --> 26:07.349
It tastes so good. My gosh.

26:19.236 --> 26:20.237
Mr. Noh?

26:21.697 --> 26:23.157
Did you come in this early?

26:24.617 --> 26:26.077
Or you didn't go home?

26:32.833 --> 26:35.336
Mr. Noh, is something wrong?

26:40.132 --> 26:41.717
On your first day here.

26:44.386 --> 26:46.847
Why did you really transfer me
to Audit Team Three?

26:54.897 --> 26:57.483
Are you still upset I put you
in charge of PM cases?

26:58.192 --> 27:01.028
I don't at all think
PM cases are trivial.

27:01.779 --> 27:03.572
You worked on enough cases to know

27:03.781 --> 27:06.992
how personal matters
can affect business matters.

27:07.701 --> 27:09.954
And they're harder to handle
because emotions are involved.

27:11.122 --> 27:12.164
I believed that

27:13.124 --> 27:16.627
with your confidence and intuition
that keep you from being swayed

27:17.753 --> 27:20.172
you'd be able to handle them well,
and I was right.

27:26.137 --> 27:27.304
Is that all?

27:28.264 --> 27:29.306
Is there really

27:31.433 --> 27:32.434
no other reason?

27:42.403 --> 27:43.445
Jei Medical Foundation.

27:44.572 --> 27:47.658
Haemu Pharma donates to them as part
of Corporate Social Responsibility.

27:48.534 --> 27:50.870
There's no problem with that.
However...

27:51.579 --> 27:52.746
They were extremely generous

27:52.830 --> 27:55.833
even when Jei Medical Foundation was
unknown and had no results to show.

28:00.629 --> 28:01.714
So...

28:01.797 --> 28:02.798
DONATIONS

28:02.882 --> 28:05.885
I kept digging
and followed lead after lead.

28:05.968 --> 28:07.136
DONATIONS MADE IN 2021

28:07.636 --> 28:10.389
JEI MEDICAL FOUNDATION:
400 MILLION WON

28:10.472 --> 28:12.600
It was awfully complicated.

28:12.683 --> 28:13.726
JEI MEDICAL FOUNDATION:
500 MILLION WON

28:14.935 --> 28:17.313
But the actual owner
of this entity is

28:21.358 --> 28:22.359
Vice President Jeon Jae-yeol.

28:23.736 --> 28:24.862
This foundation

28:26.113 --> 28:27.990
was founded by Mr. Jeon, right?

28:35.664 --> 28:36.874
Now tell me.

28:37.583 --> 28:38.834
Are they related?

28:39.543 --> 28:42.296
This case and
why you sent me to Team Three.

28:46.550 --> 28:49.303
Let's make a minor change
to your role, Mr. Noh.

28:54.183 --> 28:57.102
NOH KI-JUN, AUDIT TEAM 1 TURNOVER

28:57.186 --> 28:58.604
DELETE PERMANENTLY

29:01.398 --> 29:02.733
DO YOU WISH TO PERMANENTLY DELETE
ALL FOLDERS AND FILES?

29:02.816 --> 29:03.817
YES

29:03.901 --> 29:05.986
FOLDER WAS PERMANENTLY DELETED

29:08.822 --> 29:10.658
Yes, I halted the investigation.

29:13.619 --> 29:16.247
But I'd concluded that VP Jeon
didn't profit from the foundation

29:16.538 --> 29:19.833
nor were there issues
within Haemu Pharmaceutical.

29:19.917 --> 29:20.960
But that's...

29:21.669 --> 29:24.213
I don't think
that's for you to decide.

29:24.755 --> 29:27.007
You should've reported this
and alerted the board of executives

29:27.091 --> 29:28.717
so they could carry out
a special investigation.

29:29.593 --> 29:31.136
Shouldn't the call be made then?

29:31.220 --> 29:33.180
Things would've snowballed
unnecessarily.

29:33.722 --> 29:36.058
- It would've become political...
- And he would've gotten hurt.

29:36.850 --> 29:38.269
VP Jeon, I mean.

29:44.858 --> 29:47.528
Did he ask you to help him out?

29:49.029 --> 29:50.572
He doesn't know that I know.

29:59.623 --> 30:02.835
You're meticulous with a clear
distinction between work and life.

30:02.918 --> 30:05.087
Did you really sweep this
under the rug yourself

30:05.838 --> 30:08.299
for fear that our VP would get hurt?

30:12.177 --> 30:15.014
Even if I don't do anything,
this will come out.

30:15.514 --> 30:16.765
So do whatever it takes

30:17.683 --> 30:19.059
to be yourself

30:20.144 --> 30:21.478
and correct this.

30:28.694 --> 30:30.112
- Hi.
- Ms. Joo's here.

30:30.195 --> 30:31.739
- You came in early, Mr. Noh.
- Good morning.

30:32.740 --> 30:34.199
- Morning, Ms. Joo.
- Hello.

31:12.613 --> 31:13.822
Nice and moist.

31:14.239 --> 31:15.324
I feel refreshed.

31:24.249 --> 31:25.334
You're home.

31:28.087 --> 31:29.213
You're late.

31:34.927 --> 31:35.928
Hey.

31:36.553 --> 31:37.721
Did you drink?

32:26.645 --> 32:29.398
Hello, Chairman.
This is Joo In-a speaking.

32:31.775 --> 32:34.319
I have one additional report to make
at tomorrow's board meeting.

32:38.991 --> 32:42.744
In that case,
the last item also passed.

32:47.249 --> 32:49.543
Head of Audit,
would you like to speak?

32:51.295 --> 32:54.298
I'd like to share an additional issue
I could not previously report

32:54.923 --> 32:56.675
during the Audit Committee
here at the board meeting.

32:57.384 --> 32:59.261
One moment, Ms. Joo.

32:59.761 --> 33:02.806
There's an agenda
that wasn't presented beforehand.

33:05.601 --> 33:08.562
Director Park Sang-hwan
has something he'd like to suggest.

33:08.937 --> 33:11.273
- Please speak.
- Yes.

33:11.982 --> 33:15.152
I ask for your understanding
in this sudden discussion.

33:16.904 --> 33:20.157
The president is currently unable
to fully carry out

33:20.240 --> 33:22.951
official duties
due to health-related issues.

33:23.494 --> 33:26.997
Thus, the majority
of business decisions

33:27.080 --> 33:30.751
are solely made
by Vice President Jeon Jae-yeol.

33:31.627 --> 33:34.087
However, the president
is still standing strong.

33:34.171 --> 33:37.049
Also, his condition does not change

33:37.132 --> 33:41.428
the fact that he's our leader
and the group's anchor.

33:41.887 --> 33:46.058
On that note, in order to promote

33:46.141 --> 33:48.852
more effective decision-making
and stable management conditions

33:50.896 --> 33:55.025
I suggest appointing
Managing Director Jeon Sang-yeol

33:55.108 --> 33:56.652
as the co-vice president.

34:06.495 --> 34:07.955
What's going on with Director Park?

34:08.956 --> 34:10.290
Wasn't he with the vice president?

34:10.874 --> 34:12.459
He must've betrayed him.

34:14.628 --> 34:15.796
Silence, everyone.

34:17.589 --> 34:22.844
Now, let us vote on the agenda
which Director Park has proposed.

34:23.220 --> 34:24.888
Those who agree to appoint

34:24.972 --> 34:28.308
Managing Director Jeon Sang-yeol
as the co-vice president

34:28.392 --> 34:32.187
with Vice President Jeon Jae-yeol,
please raise your hand.

35:22.738 --> 35:23.947
Hello, Director Park.

35:24.406 --> 35:26.325
- I owe it all to you. Thank you.
- Don't mention it.

35:26.783 --> 35:28.327
I should start lining up
on his side, too.

35:38.378 --> 35:40.631
- Congratulations, Mr. Jeon.
- Ms. Joo.

35:41.673 --> 35:45.886
The sudden agenda had me flustered,
so I forgot about you.

35:46.094 --> 35:48.055
Did you say you had
another item to report on?

35:48.555 --> 35:50.891
Would you like
to report it in writing?

35:51.808 --> 35:56.104
- No, there's nothing, sir.
- All right.

35:56.563 --> 35:58.857
- Mr. Managing Director.
- Now the vice president.

35:59.316 --> 36:00.776
Goodness.

36:00.859 --> 36:02.819
Please help me out.

36:02.903 --> 36:04.946
- Why don't we go out and eat?
- Sure.

36:05.280 --> 36:06.490
Congratulations.

36:06.948 --> 36:08.158
I owe it to you.

36:10.494 --> 36:12.579
I'll need your guidance.

36:12.663 --> 36:15.248
- Goodness, you don't need that.
- I do.

36:15.624 --> 36:16.792
THE RECENT BOARD MEETING WAS INSANE

36:16.875 --> 36:18.418
THE DIRECTORS UNDER THE VP
HAVE LINED UP UNDER DIRECTOR JEON

36:18.502 --> 36:21.880
No way. So do we need approval
from two vice presidents from now on?

36:21.963 --> 36:24.633
Goodness. How will things work out
in the office?

36:24.716 --> 36:26.426
Isn't it obvious?

36:27.302 --> 36:28.387
We should side with S.

36:29.513 --> 36:31.932
I heard this
from the executive assistants.

36:32.015 --> 36:34.851
Director Park used to be
on Vice President Jeon's side

36:34.935 --> 36:36.895
but suddenly betrayed him
during this meeting.

36:37.354 --> 36:38.980
- My gosh.
- Office politics are scary.

36:40.107 --> 36:41.692
Gosh, so this is how it turned out.

36:41.775 --> 36:43.318
- What now?
- Whose side are you on?

36:43.610 --> 36:45.028
- Me?
- Yes.

36:45.445 --> 36:47.948
- I'm on your side.
- Cut it out.

36:49.241 --> 36:50.283
What about you?

36:53.745 --> 36:56.206
The report on the director... No.

37:53.430 --> 37:56.099
MR. NOH KI-JUN

38:18.705 --> 38:21.833
Your call cannot be connected.
You will be redirected to voicemail.

38:21.917 --> 38:23.418
After the beep,
you will be charged...

38:23.502 --> 38:25.378
JOO IN-A

39:01.164 --> 39:05.919
SEARCH: JOO IN-A

40:06.271 --> 40:09.774
BOO SE-YOUNG, HEAD OF HR

40:12.068 --> 40:15.363
Hey, do you realize
what time it is right now?

40:15.447 --> 40:16.573
Se-young.

40:18.074 --> 40:19.492
Can you do me a favor?

40:23.914 --> 40:26.166
You can't do this so suddenly.

40:26.249 --> 40:28.168
I thought my appointment
to the US was put on hold.

40:28.251 --> 40:30.462
Yes, for a moment
while you were unwell.

40:30.545 --> 40:31.880
You got better, so you need to go.

40:32.130 --> 40:33.632
I'm not completely well yet.

40:33.715 --> 40:35.133
I'm getting treated as an outpatient.

40:35.216 --> 40:37.344
There are hospitals in the US, too.
Don't worry.

40:37.427 --> 40:39.387
And the company will cover
all medical costs.

40:39.471 --> 40:40.597
Isn't that amazing?

40:41.514 --> 40:43.642
Does Ms. Joo know
about this sudden appointment?

40:45.393 --> 40:46.645
What do you mean?

40:46.895 --> 40:49.230
- She asked me to do this.
- Sorry?

40:49.314 --> 40:52.400
She called me early this morning
to arrange for you

40:52.484 --> 40:53.818
to go abroad as soon as possible.

40:54.152 --> 40:56.237
Instead, she asked me to give you
the special promotion now

40:56.321 --> 40:59.366
and send you to the best branch
with the easiest workload.

41:00.116 --> 41:01.117
I guess In-a

41:02.869 --> 41:04.621
really adores you.

41:15.757 --> 41:18.009
GIVING AWAY
1G OF GOLD BAR

41:26.142 --> 41:29.270
Have all these been confirmed
during the previous audit?

41:29.562 --> 41:32.190
Yes, there was also
a huge organizational change

41:32.273 --> 41:33.984
so I reprinted the sheet.

41:34.067 --> 41:35.902
Ms. Joo, may I speak with you?

41:37.570 --> 41:39.030
I'm in the middle of a report.

41:39.114 --> 41:41.032
We need to talk right now!

41:47.872 --> 41:50.208
Where are your manners,
Mr. Noh Ki-jun?

41:52.919 --> 41:54.879
Wait until Mr. Ahn is done.

42:06.349 --> 42:07.475
What do you want to talk about?

42:08.101 --> 42:09.227
You already know.

42:09.644 --> 42:10.979
What's going on
with my appointment to the US?

42:12.731 --> 42:14.524
It was already confirmed
that you were going.

42:15.066 --> 42:16.651
It's a great opportunity for you

42:16.735 --> 42:18.862
and if you're going anyway,
it's better to go soon.

42:18.945 --> 42:21.281
In the California branch,
you'll get to experience

42:21.364 --> 42:23.074
more business management
than conducting audits.

42:23.158 --> 42:25.577
Don't give me those.
What's the real reason?

42:29.664 --> 42:30.665
Is it

42:32.333 --> 42:33.543
because of Jei Medical Foundation?

42:44.971 --> 42:47.140
I'm not some kind of wuss
who can't understand that.

42:48.016 --> 42:49.350
I honestly blamed myself

42:49.434 --> 42:51.352
thinking if I had cornered you
too harshly.

42:52.228 --> 42:55.231
"Sure, when someone
you barely knew back in school

42:55.315 --> 42:57.859
suddenly shows up with a favor,
even that's difficult to turn down.

42:57.942 --> 43:00.904
So she may want to cover up
her ex-boyfriend's mishap."

43:01.571 --> 43:04.657
I thought I overreacted and regretted
getting carried away by my emotions.

43:06.910 --> 43:08.119
You didn't overreact.

43:11.206 --> 43:12.624
I can't promise you

43:15.001 --> 43:16.461
that I will right the wrong.

43:25.637 --> 43:26.846
Why not?

43:27.889 --> 43:30.850
Are you afraid
Jeon Jae-yeol will get hurt?

43:33.186 --> 43:34.437
Are you going back to him?

43:35.271 --> 43:36.606
Just as the Little Prince

43:37.107 --> 43:39.859
returned to the planet for his rose

43:40.944 --> 43:43.196
are you also going back
to Jeon Jae-yeol?

43:45.615 --> 43:47.450
- No, that's not the case.
- Then what?

43:48.868 --> 43:51.496
How am I supposed to understand
this whole situation?

43:51.913 --> 43:53.039
Do I

43:56.376 --> 43:57.794
owe you an explanation?

44:01.840 --> 44:04.425
You'll be busy getting ready to go,
so you're excused from your duties.

44:04.759 --> 44:05.927
Good luck with the preparations.

44:07.887 --> 44:09.430
INTERVIEW ROOM

44:26.364 --> 44:28.867
Hey, man. You're acting recklessly
against Ms. Joo

44:28.950 --> 44:30.577
just because
you're leaving for the US soon.

44:30.660 --> 44:32.203
Right? I was in shock.

44:32.871 --> 44:35.582
Anyway, what did you two talk about
in the interview room?

44:40.420 --> 44:43.882
Wait, we're here to celebrate him.
Why has he been downing drinks

44:43.965 --> 44:45.717
with that frown on his face?

44:45.800 --> 44:47.594
Tell me about it.
It's a great occasion.

44:48.970 --> 44:52.515
Wait, is it because
you don't want to buy us a drink?

44:52.599 --> 44:53.725
Hey, no way.

44:57.395 --> 44:58.521
Excellent.

44:58.771 --> 45:01.107
I think you should come along

45:01.858 --> 45:03.359
to the Jeju business trip, Ms. Joo.

45:04.944 --> 45:06.029
Me?

45:07.280 --> 45:08.907
What's there
for the Audit Team to do?

45:08.990 --> 45:11.326
You were with CPK and JV
while you worked abroad.

45:11.409 --> 45:14.829
You'll help break the ice
as an experienced partner.

45:15.496 --> 45:18.458
In that case, Ms. Joo must go.

45:19.375 --> 45:21.002
Gosh, I'm jealous.

45:22.045 --> 45:24.005
Jeju must be nice around this time.

45:44.651 --> 45:46.194
It's my birthday.

45:49.447 --> 45:50.865
So why don't I grab a drink?

46:18.643 --> 46:20.853
JEON JAE-YEOL
DESTINATION: JEJU

46:34.367 --> 46:36.744
Hi. Let's have a drink.
It's been a while.

46:55.054 --> 46:56.681
You heard me at the meeting, right?

46:57.181 --> 46:58.683
Get me ready
for the business trip next week.

46:58.766 --> 47:00.351
Why Ms. Joo In-a?

47:01.269 --> 47:03.771
There are more than enough reasons
for Ms. Joo In-a to accompany me.

47:03.855 --> 47:05.773
She's an experienced partner
who knows the other party.

47:05.857 --> 47:07.567
Not that, but the real reason.

47:09.444 --> 47:11.070
What do you think you're doing?

47:11.154 --> 47:13.573
No, what do you think you're doing?

47:13.656 --> 47:15.074
Not only do you get
into a drunken fight

47:15.158 --> 47:17.577
but you're sending an employee
overseas because of your feelings.

47:18.036 --> 47:20.580
Do you know
what people are saying about you?

47:20.663 --> 47:22.373
That the managing director
will become the president

47:22.457 --> 47:24.042
and you'll be kicked out.

47:24.500 --> 47:27.462
"Will he leave without causing a mess
or lose everything miserably?"

47:27.545 --> 47:29.422
They're saying
those two are the only options.

47:29.881 --> 47:31.507
In times like these

47:32.508 --> 47:35.678
why do you keep making mistakes
because of uncontained emotions?

47:36.512 --> 47:38.306
I'm used to hearing
people talk like that.

47:39.140 --> 47:40.308
And I regret

47:41.017 --> 47:42.310
letting those have an effect

47:43.061 --> 47:44.937
on acting true to my emotions.

47:47.899 --> 47:49.150
So what now?

47:49.233 --> 47:50.693
What can you do
by being true to your emotions?

47:50.777 --> 47:52.695
Are you going to die with Joo In-a?

47:52.779 --> 47:54.614
You said she was a woman
you could die with.

47:55.198 --> 47:58.117
Ms. Park A-jeong, you seem to be
the one who's emotional, not me.

47:58.201 --> 47:59.285
So?

48:00.119 --> 48:02.205
Can you even give up everything
for that woman?

48:03.206 --> 48:04.374
If I must.

48:26.479 --> 48:28.022
What are these?

48:34.695 --> 48:36.656
Why did I get this?
I never even use it.

48:38.074 --> 48:41.619
From now on, I swear
to live as a minimalist.

48:45.498 --> 48:46.916
Hey, just leave those.

48:47.291 --> 48:49.961
I'm sure there are dishes in the US.
You can use them.

48:51.254 --> 48:54.882
Anyway, come to think of it,
I'm glad you moved in here.

48:55.341 --> 48:58.845
It would've been too much work
to rent out the place while I'm gone.

49:02.432 --> 49:04.392
Hey, are you listening?

49:05.143 --> 49:06.394
Ki-jun.

49:06.894 --> 49:08.813
Do you know that
the vice president and Joo In-a

49:09.605 --> 49:11.607
are going to Jeju next week?

49:13.943 --> 49:16.529
I do. I saw the schedule.

49:17.488 --> 49:21.117
They've traveled there together.

49:21.868 --> 49:24.245
It must be such a dear memory.

49:24.495 --> 49:26.664
He even kept the old plane ticket.

49:29.792 --> 49:31.335
Sounds humble.

49:31.961 --> 49:34.338
I didn't know even rich people
like him go to Jeju as a couple.

49:38.092 --> 49:40.470
Hey, I said you can use that cup.

49:42.054 --> 49:43.514
Did you pack all these?

49:44.432 --> 49:46.934
Just leave these dishes
back in the cupboard.

49:54.066 --> 49:55.318
Are you okay?

50:01.324 --> 50:03.576
I'll get it. That must be our food.

50:21.761 --> 50:22.845
Ki-jun.

50:47.119 --> 50:49.956
I'll step out for a moment.
We're out of drinking water.

50:50.039 --> 50:51.749
- Okay. Sure.
- Excuse me.

51:00.508 --> 51:02.718
What? Why? Did I do anything wrong?

51:02.802 --> 51:05.221
I just explained everything.
She's renting out a room from me.

51:07.431 --> 51:08.933
Stop pinching me, will you?

51:10.560 --> 51:13.354
Hey, what is wrong with you?

51:13.437 --> 51:15.106
You kept a woman
by your side at the hospital

51:15.189 --> 51:16.649
but actually live with another?

51:16.732 --> 51:18.025
Who do you think you are?

51:18.109 --> 51:21.070
I'm a nobody. Okay?
But you know what?

51:23.364 --> 51:24.574
That woman isn't into me.

51:25.741 --> 51:27.743
What kind of nonsense is this?

51:27.827 --> 51:30.705
Hey. How could she do that
if she wasn't into you?

51:32.206 --> 51:34.667
I don't know, but she said
she likes another man.

51:34.750 --> 51:35.960
So you forget about her, too.

51:38.629 --> 51:41.090
You foolish idiot!

51:41.173 --> 51:43.801
You can't just take her words
and take it as is.

51:43.884 --> 51:46.929
Pay attention to her demeanor,
actions, and look in her eyes!

51:47.013 --> 51:50.683
Think of the way she looked at you
while you were at the hospital.

51:50.766 --> 51:53.936
Good grief. You're so slow.

53:46.757 --> 53:49.885
Oddly enough, I have a habit

53:51.095 --> 53:53.180
of hiding the truth
when it matters most.

54:15.970 --> 54:18.389
- Hey.
- Where are they staying in Jeju?

54:18.973 --> 54:21.100
- What?
- Where's Joo In-a staying in Jeju?

54:21.684 --> 54:24.354
Why? Are you going to go after her?

54:24.437 --> 54:26.022
I'm asking you! Where is she?

54:28.775 --> 54:30.318
Jeon Jae-yeol, Noh Ki-jun.

54:32.403 --> 54:33.946
You're both insane.

54:48.503 --> 54:51.589
The terms don't look so bad
though you'll need to verify.

54:52.465 --> 54:54.717
I'd prefer the investment
to be bigger.

54:55.551 --> 54:57.428
But a higher risk
will come with that.

54:57.512 --> 54:59.555
CPK is just a money-lending business.

54:59.639 --> 55:00.681
There's no soul.

55:08.272 --> 55:09.482
It's nice to be here with you.

55:14.237 --> 55:15.446
Jeju, I mean.

55:16.823 --> 55:20.034
It was our first and last trip.

55:21.786 --> 55:24.622
We managed to take a leave
at the same time and come here

55:25.790 --> 55:27.834
but only worked the whole time
just like we're doing now.

55:32.255 --> 55:34.382
The biggest concern now
is the formation of the board.

55:34.465 --> 55:35.466
In-a.

55:40.888 --> 55:43.141
Mr. Vice President, it seems like
you're having a hard time focusing.

55:44.267 --> 55:46.769
I'll look over this separately
and report back to you.

55:46.853 --> 55:48.187
Wait, In-a.

55:50.148 --> 55:51.399
Can we sit here...

55:53.401 --> 55:55.153
like the old days for a moment?

56:02.326 --> 56:03.744
That's not going to happen.

56:05.455 --> 56:07.081
We can't go back
to how things used to be.

56:07.748 --> 56:09.542
Then why did you return to Korea?

56:21.012 --> 56:22.054
To honor what I said.

56:23.806 --> 56:25.892
I promised to take your side.

56:27.268 --> 56:28.895
So this is the last I can do
to honor my words.

56:28.978 --> 56:30.229
That's more than enough.

56:30.313 --> 56:32.773
I don't care how you feel
and why you're doing it.

56:34.442 --> 56:35.985
Please just stay by my side.

56:37.403 --> 56:38.571
That's all I need.

56:45.828 --> 56:47.288
I'm done doing that, too.

56:49.081 --> 56:50.666
I got caught up with that promise

56:53.252 --> 56:55.004
and made a mistake I shouldn't have.

56:58.007 --> 56:59.717
And I hurt someone.

57:02.553 --> 57:04.138
I shouldn't have done that to him.

57:08.392 --> 57:09.977
Are you talking about Mr. Noh Ki-jun?

57:22.281 --> 57:23.616
What I'm trying to say is

57:25.159 --> 57:27.328
I'm never going back to you,
Jae-yeol.

58:53.873 --> 58:55.499
It must be far too late

58:56.792 --> 58:58.002
to go to you.

59:04.884 --> 59:06.052
Joo In-a!

59:29.992 --> 59:31.243
Joo In-a!

59:48.719 --> 59:49.845
Noh Ki-jun.

01:00:05.778 --> 01:00:08.114
Why did you check out already?

